  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=4x-2y,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the $2$-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton method. Given that the step size is $\u0394x=\\frac{1}{4},$ and that the first step has already been computed using the Runge-Kutta method, fill the missing entries in the table below, where ${y}_{p}$ denotes the predictor at each step.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\u0394{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |",
